# Deploy path

Default: **commit → `git push origin main` → GitHub Actions → VPS**.

If Actions fails (empty SSH secrets, etc.) or the user asks to deploy/restart: do it yourself over SSH — do not wait for the user to run deploy.

```bash
# from sanskrit_srv/
rsync -az --delete \
  --exclude '.git/' --exclude 'docs/' --exclude '.env' --exclude '.env.*' \
  --exclude 'storage/' --exclude 'data/' --exclude '.venv/' \
  --exclude '__pycache__/' --exclude '*.pyc' --exclude '.github/' --exclude '.cursor/' \
  ./ freevpn:/opt/sanskrit_srv/
ssh freevpn 'bash /opt/sanskrit_srv/deploy/remote_deploy.sh'
# remote_deploy.sh restarts sanskrit-srv + sanskrit-worker; verify:
ssh freevpn 'curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8000/health'
```

- Host alias: `freevpn` → `root@72.56.99.56`, app at `/opt/sanskrit_srv`.
- Keep git and VPS in sync: push to GitHub even when you also rsync.
- Never commit `.env`, `storage/`, or `data/`.
